message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Universal Threshold Activation Criticality (UTAC): Emergent Steepness Framework"
abstract: >-
  The Universal Threshold Activation Criticality (UTAC) framework establishes a
  unified field-theoretic approach to critical transitions across domains. This
  repository contains the complete implementation of UTAC v2.0, including:
  (1) microscopic derivation of β≈4.2 from Renormalization Group theory,
  (2) field type classification with type-conditioned meta-regressions (R²=0.665),
  (3) spectral analysis via Fourier decomposition for emergent pattern recognition,
  (4) validation pipeline with agent-based modeling and cross-domain empirical tests,
  (5) arXiv-ready manuscript "Emergent Steepness" with figures and supplementary materials.
  The framework foregrounds the quartet (R, Θ, β, ζ(R)) and the sigmoid response
  σ(β(R-Θ)) governing phase transitions in physics, climate, cognition, and AI systems.
  Version 2.0 elevates UTAC from phenomenological observation to theoretically grounded
  framework with predictive power across 36 validated systems in 11 domains.
